{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-42579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $|{A}^{-1}|,$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 & -3 \\\\ -12 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-42579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 & -3 \\\\ -12 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}=-\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-42579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "93b17d77ad9debc5750208bbfd731b455b90edce9e2652bf69d3f0ab2faafc3c"} {"question" "q-42579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-42579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{21}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{13}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-42579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-43097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$|\\begin{aligned}107 & 215 & 99 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 11 \\\\ 107 & 215 & 100\\end{aligned}|=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-43097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the $1$st row of our determinant is almost equal to the $3$rd row. So, we can rewrite the given determinant, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}107 & 215 & 99 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 11 \\\\ 107 & 215 & 100\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}107 & 215 & 99 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 11 \\\\ 107+0 & 215+0 & 99+1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}107 & 215 & 99 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 11 \\\\ 107+0 & 215+0 & 99+1\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}107 & 215 & 99 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 11 \\\\ 107 & 215 & 99\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}107 & 215 & 99 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first determinant must be zero since it has two identical rows, while the second determinant can be expanded across the $3$rd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}107 & 215 & 99 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 11 \\\\ 107 & 215 & 99\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}107 & 215 & 99 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0+1(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}107 & 215 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =107\\cdot 8-215\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =-434\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-43097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "93b17d77ad9debc5750208bbfd731b455b90edce9e2652bf69d3f0ab2faafc3c"} {"question" "q-43097" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-43097" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-424"] ["math" "-434"] ["math" "2\\,146"] ["math" "440"] ["math" "870"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-43097" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-434"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-88301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find\n$|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 91 & 92 & 93 \\\\ 90 & 92 & 93\\end{aligned}|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-88301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the $2$nd row of our determinant is almost equal to the $3$rd row. So, we can rewrite the given determinant, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 91 & 92 & 93 \\\\ 90 & 92 & 93\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 90+1 & 92+0 & 93+0 \\\\ 90 & 92 & 93\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 90+1 & 92+0 & 93+0 \\\\ 90 & 92 & 93\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 90 & 92 & 93 \\\\ 90 & 92 & 93\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 90 & 92 & 93\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first determinant must be zero since it has two identical rows, while the second determinant can be expanded across the $2$nd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 90 & 92 & 93 \\\\ 90 & 92 & 93\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 90 & 92 & 93\\end{aligned}| & =0+1(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 92 & 93\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(3\\cdot 93-6\\cdot 92) \\\\  & =-(279-552) \\\\  & =273\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-88301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "93b17d77ad9debc5750208bbfd731b455b90edce9e2652bf69d3f0ab2faafc3c"} {"question" "q-88301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-88301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "273"] ["math" "282"] ["math" "327"] ["math" "372"] ["math" "447"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-88301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "273"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-88304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find\n$|\\begin{aligned}97 & 98 & 99 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 96 & 98 & 99\\end{aligned}|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-88304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the $1$st row of our determinant is almost equal to the $3$rd row. So, we can rewrite the given determinant, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}97 & 98 & 99 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 96 & 98 & 99\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}96+1 & 98+0 & 99+0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 96 & 98 & 99\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}96+1 & 98+0 & 99+0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 96 & 98 & 99\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}96 & 98 & 99 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 96 & 98 & 99\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 96 & 98 & 99\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first determinant must be zero since it has two identical rows, while the second determinant can be expanded across the $1$st row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}96 & 98 & 99 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 96 & 98 & 99\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 96 & 98 & 99\\end{aligned}| & =0+1(-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 98 & 99\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot 99-2\\cdot 98 \\\\  & =396-196 \\\\  & =200\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-88304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "93b17d77ad9debc5750208bbfd731b455b90edce9e2652bf69d3f0ab2faafc3c"} {"question" "q-88304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-88304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "192"] ["math" "200"] ["math" "202"] ["math" "204"] ["math" "210"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-88304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "200"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-130631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ be square matrices. If $A=B\\cdot C,$  $|B|=-15$ and $|{C}^{-1}|=3$, find $|A|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-130631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nAlso, given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $M,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({M}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(M)}.\n$$\n\nSince $|C|=\\frac{1}{|{C}^{-1}|}$, we get $|C|=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|B|\\cdot |C| \\\\  & =(-15)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/state.json" "file_sha256" "353a206752ec0cd18c77afa06fd96b73b249e8cacc37b621aada85894943ae11"} {"question" "q-130631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068620/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "93b17d77ad9debc5750208bbfd731b455b90edce9e2652bf69d3f0ab2faafc3c"} 